No — a personal GitHub account doesn't have user/role management at all. That feature only exists at the Organization level.

What you can do on a personal account:

• Add Collaborators to individual repos (Repo → Settings → Collaborators → Add people)

• Collaborators get simple permission levels per repo: Read, Triage, Write, Maintain, Admin (same list as before)

• That's it — no teams, no org-wide roles, no centralized member management

What you can't do:

• No "invite member to account" concept
• No Owner/Member split
• No Teams
• No org-wide 2FA enforcement policy
• No SSO/SAML enforcement

